# The log of the test must have a line for each of these patterns (grep -E).
\[2\.50\].* surfaces Ladder count=174
# First ladder. The player starts on the floor.
\[4\.00\].* JCDentonMale0 .* loc=\(-6384 1420 -243\)
# With the walk key and a level view, the player goes up the ladder to the ceiling of the room.
\[6\.00\].* JCDentonMale0 .* loc=\(-6384 1479 -172\) .*Physics=PHYS_Walking
# With no key down, the player stays on the ladder.
\[8\.00\].* JCDentonMale0 .* loc=\(-6384 1479 -172\)
# With the view down and the walk key, the player goes down to the floor.
\[8\.70\].* ViewRotation=\(Pitch=(49|50)[0-9][0-9][0-9], Yaw=16384, Roll=0\)
\[10\.00\].* JCDentonMale0 .* loc=\(-6384 1479 -244\)
# Second ladder. It starts above the floor, so the walk key alone does not start the climb.
\[12\.50\].* JCDentonMale0 .* loc=\(7705 -2804 -419\) .*Physics=PHYS_Walking
# After a jump, the player is on the ladder and goes up. The physics mode stays the falling mode, as in the original.
\[14\.50\].* JCDentonMale0 .* loc=\(7704 -2804 -348\) .*Physics=PHYS_Falling
\[16\.00\].* JCDentonMale0 .* loc=\(7704 -2804 -348\) .*Physics=PHYS_Falling
# The jump gives no script warning: a player on level geometry has the level as its base.
!Accessed None
